    "c16d1c6a-ec39-427a-bbad-9c0b612d774d": {
      "id": "c16d1c6a-ec39-427a-bbad-9c0b612d774d",
      "message": {
        "author": {
          "name": null,
          "role": "assistant"
        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "I'd keep it warm, personal, and still appropriate for the relationship between a leader and a team member.\n\n> Aanchal, that honestly means so much to me. \u2764\ufe0f Thank you for trusting me with that. I'm very similar. I tend to keep my personal life private too, so I completely understand where you're coming from.\n>\n> I just want to make sure I never see you as \"just an employee.\" You're a huge part of what we're building, and more importantly, you're a person first. If life ever gets heavy, or if you just need someone to listen, my door is always open. There will never be any pressure to share more than you're comfortable with, but I always want you to know you don't have to carry things alone.\n>\n> I'm really looking forward to spending some time together next week, getting to know you beyond work. And thank you for your kind words. Watching you grow has been one of the best parts of building this company, and I'm incredibly grateful to have you on this journey with us. \u2764\ufe0f\n\nThis keeps healthy boundaries while reinforcing that you genuinely care about her as a person, not just as an employee. It also naturally builds trust without feeling overly formal."
          ]
        },
